# System design stays current

- Update `docs/agents/system-design.md` in the same PR when your change touches anything in its section 12 table ("Keeping the docs current").
- Keep its Mermaid diagrams. Update a diagram when a part, store, external service, or deploy target is added or removed. Never replace a diagram with prose.
- Keep it readable by someone new: plain words, and a glossary line for any new term.
- Link to a fact's home instead of copying it (tick order: `code-flow.md`; rules: `CONSTRAINTS.md`; honest limits: `team-manifest.md`).
- Update `docs/humans/system-design.md` only if the one-minute picture changed.
- `tests/test_system_design.py` fails when a setting in `.env.example`, a dependency, a dataclass in `server/engine/contracts.py`, or a Render service is missing from the doc, or when a diagram is deleted.

The design itself lives in `docs/agents/system-design.md`. Read it there; do not copy it here.
